  "Enable free look": "",
  "Look around without turning your character. Off restores stock camera behavior entirely.": "",
  "Free look key": "",
  "Held down to look around. Left Alt is the usual binding for this in other games. None = off.": "",
  "Toggle instead of hold": "",
  "Tap to enter free look and tap again to leave, rather than holding. Easy to forget you left it on.": "",
  "Double tap to latch": "",
  "Holding still works, but a quick double tap latches free look on and another releases it. It is also the only way in on a controller, where the game\u0027s auto-walk button - left stick click - latches it too.": "",
  "Recall key": "",
  "Tapped to swing the view back to where you were last looking. It remembers the DIRECTION, not the angle, so it still finds the same place after you have turned - as far as Look range allows. Works while looking around, and on its own: a tap engages free look and goes there. Tapping it again ends it, and so does the free look key. Forgotten when you change region. None = off.": "",
  "Feel": "",
  "Look range": "",
  "How far the view may swing from your direction of travel, to each side. 180 is straight behind you, about what neck, eyes and a twist from the hips can manage. The slider goes further for a view the body could not deliver.": "",
  "Return speed": "",
  "How fast the view swings back once released, in degrees per second. A glance comes back promptly and a full swing takes proportionally longer. Zero snaps instantly.\n\nFor scale, a relaxed look around is about 150\u00B0/s and the fastest a person can swing their gaze is roughly 800\u00B0/s.": "",
  "Focus View": "",
  "Enable focus view": "",
  "Hold a second key to zoom in on whatever you are looking at. By default it works only while you are already looking around, the two being halves of one gesture; the setting below frees it.": "",
  "Focus key": "",
  "Held down to zoom. The default is the middle mouse button, which the game itself leaves unbound - note that Unity calls it Mouse2, not Mouse3. Right mouse is not offered: it aims, throws a torch or flare, or switches a flashlight to high beam. None = off.": "",
  "Toggle focus instead of holding": "",
  "Tap to zoom in and tap again to come back out, rather than holding. It still ends by itself whenever you could not have started it, such as raising a weapon or opening a menu.": "",
  "Focus without free look": "",
  "Lets the focus key zoom on its own, with the view still facing the way you are walking. Off means it only works while you are already looking around.": "",
  "Zoom amount": "",
  "How far focus view zooms in. The game\u0027s own zoom when aiming is about 1.43x, for reference. Look sensitivity drops by the same factor, so the view does not turn twitchy at the far end.": "",
  "Zoom time": "",
  "How long the zoom takes to arrive, and to leave again.\n\nWhen free look ENDS while you are still zoomed, the zoom ignores this and follows the view home instead, so the two arrive together.": "",
  "Edge darkening": "",
  "Darkens the edges of the screen while you are focused. It is the game\u0027s own edge darkening turned up slightly, so the shape is one you already know, and it fades in and out with the zoom.": "",
  "Foveal blur": "",
  "Sharp in the middle of the screen and blurring gently toward the edges, the way your own vision works. How much of the screen blurs is fixed rather than adjustable.": "",
  "Arms": "",
  "Show held item while looking": "",
  "Keeps your held item on screen while you look around. It will look wrong: these models are built for a forward view only, so expect hollow cut edges, geometry ending in mid-air, and the camera passing inside the mesh.": "",
  "Hide beyond": "",
  "How far you may look, either way, before the held item is hidden after all. At 180 it is never hidden.": "",
  "Indicator Icon": "",
  "Show icon": "",
  "When the free look icon appears on the HUD:\nWhenever looking - key held or latched\nWhile latched - only when locked on\nNever - not at all": "",
  "Whenever looking": "",
